CONTROL 2 — the contrast threshold raised to 7.0:1 (WCAG AAA)

The four verdict colours measured on screen are 5.12–6.75:1, which clears AA (4.5:1) and not AAA.
Driving the same walk with inv.AA_CONTRAST monkey-patched to 7.0 must convict all four. This is
the arm that proves the ratios are read from the page rather than reported from a constant.

$ /tmp/ctrl2.py  (imports walk_release, patches check_site_invariants.AA_CONTRAST = 7.0)

--- ctrl2.py --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
"""Control 2: the SAME clean release, with the contrast floor raised from 4.5 to 7.0.
Every measured ratio is under 7, so a live comparison must report all four. If the arm reported
nothing, the ratios would not be reaching any comparison at all.
"""
import sys
sys.path.insert(0, "platform/build")
import check_site_invariants as inv
import walk_release
inv.AA_CONTRAST = 7.0
raise SystemExit(walk_release.main(["--prefix", "/v/20260917T091943Z"]))

